{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods","id":559551,"title":"Novas v. Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T10:45:43-07:00","id":559551,"title":"Novas v. Gods","content":"From the 3rd teaser tag: &quot;On the other hand, I imagine the gods themselves feel a bit limited next to Divis Mal or the Colony.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do people think about this? Should supervillains make gods feel &quot;limited&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:08:12-07:00","id":559571,"title":"","content":"Hopefully tag, which will die in further development. It really does not work in concept of Scion themes and power levels and hopefully springs from not understanding Scion gods, and going with vague definition of gods, as powerful beings , instead of pillars of reality high end gods are in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:40:00-07:00","id":559616,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this helps but, from what I've heard, this &quot;Divis Mal&quot; guy is a real Samuel Haight sort of NPC. You know the kind; they're the ones with a &quot;I Win&quot; button as a statblock and have adventures with them in it themed around the idea of &quot;PCs watch the cool guy do cool things!&quot;, so he's probably not a proper presentation of power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:50:36-07:00","id":559628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559616#post559616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this helps but, from what I've heard, this &quot;Divis Mal&quot; guy is a real Samuel Haight sort of NPC. You know the kind; they're the ones with a &quot;I Win&quot; button as a statblock and have adventures with them in it themed around the idea of &quot;PCs watch the cool guy do cool things!&quot;, so he's probably not a proper presentation of power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it does not work at all and special snowflake NPC fiasco is dead trend,which development evolved beyond. Bigger problem is actually Colony, who is actual final boss(one of) of the setting and should be fightable by beings under the level of heroes, which is just no. He is also just one of the many beings of the same power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:36:45-07:00","id":559676,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't read too much into comparisons between the two universes right now. The benchmarks we're using only take into account internal playtesting, and we haven't brought actual powers into play yet, which are going to make a big difference in what characters can accomplish and what areas they can compete in.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not an arms race between Trinity and Scion. They're based on the same engine, but aren't being designed for PvP versus each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:53:48-07:00","id":559714,"title":"","content":"It does kinda bode ill since it gives some insight into the writers' ideas of relative scale, though. Though, there was that Quantum 10 power: Create Universe, where Divis Mal build the World of Darkness or something... the 90s was an odd time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:05:44-07:00","id":559733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559676#post559676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't read too much into comparisons between the two universes right now. The benchmarks we're using only take into account internal playtesting, and we haven't brought actual powers into play yet, which are going to make a big difference in what characters can accomplish and what areas they can compete in.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not an arms race between Trinity and Scion. They're based on the same engine, but aren't being designed for PvP versus each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>With revelation(more confirmation), that Sardonyx is primarily Narrativist(Cinematic) System, this does not work. Words and tiers are what drives Cinematic systems, rolls are important, but secondary and powers are just icing on the cake -cool things, that tell me about my character, but do not truly define him and his strength in the setting, as does Simulationist system. With this in mind, you keep creating these issues and then using this as defense, but these are the core issues of the system, which should have been ironed out, before you started writing math, because that is the core of Narativistic system, not powers, but tiers and themes and their interactions. Math is subservient to that.<br /> <br /> Also Stronger, than Scion god is an Issue for Trinity,not Scion which you did not adress, something stronger, than Scion god, should not be fightable by Psions, who simply hardcore lack umph to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:56:12-07:00","id":559765,"title":"","content":"Maybe Psions can jump effective tiers by working in teams? Let them have powers that manipulate scales slightly for certain effects, have the powers stack, and I can see a lone Psion struggling against a Hero when a squad of five manages to curbstomp a demigod through synergetic power use (which I thought was how Psions were meant to take down Novas). I agree that I don't think novas should hit god level until a long way into their development, but scale manipulation might let Psions even the odds.<br /> <br /> This sounds like an interesting idea for a purview, if you remove the stacking part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:09:24-07:00","id":559796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559765#post559765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Psions can jump effective tiers by working in teams? Let them have powers that manipulate scales slightly for certain effects, have the powers stack, and I can see a lone Psion struggling against a Hero when a squad of five manages to curbstomp a demigod through synergetic power use (which I thought was how Psions were meant to take down Novas). I agree that I don't think novas should hit god level until a long way into their development, but scale manipulation might let Psions even the odds.<br /> <br /> This sounds like an interesting idea for a purview, if you remove the stacking part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really problem with synergistic use of powers, (outside of how potentially boring it is), that tier jumping and/or similar adding effects will hard kill simple math, this type of system needs to work and potentially returns us to broken high level. It also kinda breaks promise of simple math.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:14:48-07:00","id":559800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559796#post559796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really problem with synergistic use of powers, (outside of how potentially boring it is), that tier jumping and/or similar adding effects will hard kill simple math, this type of system needs to work and potentially returns us to broken high level. It also kinda breaks promise of simple math.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I forgot most people prefer simple maths (I love the complex stuff), I still think Psions should actually be given synergistic powers though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:36:04-07:00","id":559808,"title":"","content":"Gods in Scion have never shown to be as powerful as high end novas in Aberrant; that's just how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T14:58:40-07:00","id":559822,"title":"","content":"That depends. The Ultimates and Avatars certainly seem to suggest otherwise. But then there's that Create Universe power lurking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:01:53-07:00","id":559823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559822#post559822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends. The Ultimates and Avatars certainly seem to suggest otherwise. But then there's that Create Universe power lurking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesnt god gets mini universe, if they decide to buy it? and universe creation really does not work in cosmology of Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:02:44-07:00","id":559827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559733#post559733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With revelation(more confirmation), that Sardonyx is primarily Narrativist(Cinematic) System, this does not work. Words and tiers are what drives Cinematic systems, rolls are important, but secondary and powers are just icing on the cake -cool things, that tell me about my character, but do not truly define him and his strength in the setting, as does Simulationist system. With this in mind, you keep creating these issues and then using this as defense, but these are the core issues of the system, which should have been ironed out, before you started writing math, because that is the core of Narativistic system, not powers, but tiers and themes and their interactions. Math is subservient to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to take a straw poll, but I don't believe any of Sardonyx's designers believe the Usenet/Forge model of game design (Narrativist/Simulationist/Gamist) to be worth the pixels it takes up.<br /> <br /> We wanted to do for scalable action/adventure genre games as Storytelling does for street-level horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:06:07-07:00","id":559828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559823#post559823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesnt god gets mini universe, if they decide to buy it? and universe creation really does not work in cosmology of Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact that pretty much every pantheon has one or more deities that did EXACTLY that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:08:44-07:00","id":559830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559828#post559828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the fact that pretty much every pantheon has one or more deities that did EXACTLY that.</div> </div> </div> </div>and that is reason we speak about Scion gods:/ .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:16:29-07:00","id":559838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559808#post559808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods in Scion have never shown to be as powerful as high end novas in Aberrant; that's just how it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't buy that. There are a very limited number of the high end novas and they are particularized as to powers. In Scion there are nigh on 30 gods out of the subset of deities with formal descriptions from the pantheons from the sourcebooks (not including Atlantean or WW2) which are an even smaller subset of the pantheons with enough mythology to have a clue about who can use Ultimate Strength to do things like, say, rip apart the Pillars of Gibraltar, manhandle a snake that circles the world, hold up the sky, chop the valley of Nepal into the Himalayas, etc. etc. And almost all of them can do a half-dozen OTHER equally super-potent things as well. <br /> <br /> Aside from Create Universe, there are few novas (if any really) who can claim that level of might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:19:40-07:00","id":559845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559827#post559827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have to take a straw poll, but I don't believe any of Sardonyx's designers believe the Usenet/Forge model of game design (Narrativist/Simulationist/Gamist) to be worth the pixels it takes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's a lot more important for video games, where you don't have a made-of-meat person there to adjudicate weirdness on the fly. For tabletop, though, the only real question for me as an ST is, &quot;how much work do the rules make me do?&quot; When I have to fight the rules, that's a problem. So far, to me, Sardonyx looks great. My only concern is actually that the high-end tier differences might be too much even at the PC/main character level. If (forex) Titans get +9 against high-end Gods who are just one Tier below them...well, let's just say I ran that Scion campaign, and house-ruled the frack out of it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I never thought I'd play Scion again (I have <i>way</i> too many ideas, and already ran a several-year campaign from Hero to God), but Sardonyx has me excited. OTOH, I'm already looking at the possibilities of a Trinity/Scion mashup, which would take things in a more traditional supers-y direction, so I'll confess to hoping that &quot;not an arms race&quot; (which I agree with entirely, BTW) doesn't equal &quot;crossovers won't really work.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:36:25-07:00","id":559859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods#post559551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the 3rd teaser tag: &quot;On the other hand, I imagine the gods themselves feel a bit limited next to Divis Mal or the Colony.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do people think about this? Should supervillains make gods feel &quot;limited&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aii-yaaaa.<br /> <br /> I was mostly making an example to describe the Scale system for individuals like the Colony (who nebulously create entire species from themselves, and may or may not be a Necromorph moon) and Divis Mal (who, yes, creates universes and takes his ball and goes home) compared to Hermes or even Bishamonten/Vi\u015brava\u1e47a. And that guy's a king.<br /> <br /> If you like, put Fenris, J\u00f6rmungandr, World Turtle, or Damballa around the same level. It's not meant to describe a ceiling, only an <i>extremely rough </i>benchmark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 06-18-2015, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:09:52-07:00","id":559943,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that, potentially, you could use the Aberrant scale to deal with Those Gods. The folks like Odin who have power that few, if any, gods achieve. Not quite Titans, but significantly more powerful than the standard deity. <br /> <br /> Most pantheons would have a limited number of them. The Hindu Trimurti would have that scale, as would the Four Tezcatlipocas. Eshu may be the only one of the orisha to qualify, only Shango really compares, and he's scared shitless of Eshu. Zeus would have that scale, and maybe Poseidon and Hades as well. Ra USED to be at that scale, then he had to tell Isis his True Name or die. <br /> <br /> Just a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":267,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","user":"griffinguy24","date":". 06-18-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:51:19-07:00","id":560041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559859#post559859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aii-yaaaa.<br /> <br /> I was mostly making an example to describe the Scale system for individuals like the Colony (who nebulously create entire species from themselves, and may or may not be a Necromorph moon) and Divis Mal (who, yes, creates universes and takes his ball and goes home) compared to Hermes or even Bishamonten/Vi\u015brava\u1e47a. And that guy's a king.<br /> <br /> If you like, put Fenris, J\u00f6rmungandr, World Turtle, or Damballa around the same level. It's not meant to describe a ceiling, only an <i>extremely rough </i>benchmark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that comes across as &quot;Yeah, Thor will always suck compared to Superman&quot; type of thing.<br /> <br /> If you chopped down Epic Attributes to a 1-6 system, there's a lot less 'big jump' on scales. Even at the lower level, the +1, +2 or +4 is not that disrupting. Going from Epic5 (+11) to Epic 6 (+15) is a lot lower tier in jump than I think I see in the Tier system and it scales more evenly across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:13:45-07:00","id":560719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods#post559551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the 3rd teaser tag: &quot;On the other hand, I imagine the gods themselves feel a bit limited next to Divis Mal or the Colony.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do people think about this? Should supervillains make gods feel &quot;limited&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder Woman versus Superman? I read that comic back in the 1970's!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:23:51-07:00","id":560899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=560719#post560719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wonder Woman versus Superman? I read that comic back in the 1970's!</div> </div> </div> </div>More recently, Apollo tried zapping Superman right in the face. This backfired horribly, because Superman is solar-powered, and punched Apollo through a mountain. Nowadays, Superman Vs. Wonder Woman usually ends in make-up sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:57:26-07:00","id":560916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=560899#post560899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More recently, Apollo tried zapping Superman right in the face. This backfired horribly, because Superman is solar-powered, and punched Apollo through a mountain. Nowadays, Superman Vs. Wonder Woman usually ends in make-up sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Apollo or Thor or Ares or Pluto in the comics usually doesn't resemble the most common amalgamation or archetype of the deity of that name. And I'm not talking in appearance (e.g. the superficial read that can end up with blonde instead of red hair). The power wielded by the gods in myths is transcendent. Transcendent power in comics becomes boring if it's not mostly offstage or its something that has to dealt with. Comic book protagonists who start demonstrating mythological god-like levels of power are de-powered. It's harder to tell an interesting story in genre when your protagonist meets your antagonist and wins without any conflict. You can't keep a title going with a near-ominpotent hero facing his near-omnipotent nemesis all the time (with occasional encounters with foes that serve as Swifters...) <br /> <br /> Apollo IS the sun. The sun is his chariot. Both are true at the same time without being contradictory. He is disease and healing and poetry and rational thought. At that's the short list of the highlights of what Apollo brings to the table. <br /> <br /> Superman is effectively a pre-godhood flying Heracles who can project heat and cold.... Sorta anime-Heracles. Or wu-xia Heracles. <br /> <br /> At best Novas, seem to have be effectively the same as most mythologies' Demigods (with a very few exceptions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:53:06-07:00","id":560936,"title":"","content":"It would probably make more sense if they are talking about flexibility.<br /> That is to say, not that Divis Mal could beat up a Scion God.<br /> But that Divis Mal has great deal of freedom to make his own choices while being incredibly powerful, where Scion Gods are more restricted through fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:59:24-07:00","id":561232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=560916#post560916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Apollo or Thor or Ares or Pluto in the comics usually doesn't resemble the most common amalgamation or archetype of the deity of that name. And I'm not talking in appearance (e.g. the superficial read that can end up with blonde instead of red hair). The power wielded by the gods in myths is transcendent. Transcendent power in comics becomes boring if it's not mostly offstage or its something that has to dealt with. Comic book protagonists who start demonstrating mythological god-like levels of power are de-powered. It's harder to tell an interesting story in genre when your protagonist meets your antagonist and wins without any conflict. You can't keep a title going with a near-ominpotent hero facing his near-omnipotent nemesis all the time (with occasional encounters with foes that serve as Swifters...)<br /> <br /> Apollo IS the sun. The sun is his chariot. Both are true at the same time without being contradictory. He is disease and healing and poetry and rational thought. At that's the short list of the highlights of what Apollo brings to the table.<br /> <br /> Superman is effectively a pre-godhood flying Heracles who can project heat and cold.... Sorta anime-Heracles. Or wu-xia Heracles.<br /> <br /> At best Novas, seem to have be effectively the same as most mythologies' Demigods (with a very few exceptions).</div> </div> </div> </div>No disrespect, when was the last time you read a comicbook? The last 10-15 years have seen a <u><b>lot</b></u> of change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T08:54:10-07:00","id":561967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=561232#post561232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No disrespect, when was the last time you read a comicbook? The last 10-15 years have seen a <u><b>lot</b></u> of change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm..... I've been collecting comics for over 40 years. I have files cabinets full of them. I also have advanced degrees in anthropology with an emphasis in comparative mythology. I would argue very emphatically that there has been LESS change in the past 10-15 years than there was between the two decades before that.. <br /> <br /> I stand by what I said EXACTLY. The example given was: Superman gets charged up by Apollo's &quot;sun blast&quot; and uses the energy to punch him through a mountain. In what way does that represent Superman as anything other than what I said he was while simultaneously not representing Apollo as anything other than another type of similar super-being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:26:20-07:00","id":562005,"title":"","content":"Its worth mentioning that the introduction of deities to comic books in Marvels Thor was originally intended by Stan Lee (First of his name) to explicitly be better than Superman could ever be and frankly to kick his ass all over the place. The entire inspiration was &quot;What could be more powerful than Superman? Someone who isn't a Man at all, but a living God&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, this runs into reality when large segments of the populace are uncomfortable with letting their children read about and Idealize other Deities and the general fact that Superman is the most popular hero in the world, at the end of the day narrative reality bows to that other super powerful green item.<br /> <br /> I'll also bring up the fact that Superman and many other comic book characters are religious in some vague manner (I think Superman might be a Methodist, the Thing is Jewish, etc). that means they acknowledge the presence of Deities, that they are more powerful than them and even deserving of worship from them. That kinda solidifies the issue in my mind as the Deities in Scion are not literary figures who happen to have taken an ancient name, but the honest to goodness Gods of the worlds religions. (Including the ones superheros might worship)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:23:15-07:00","id":562439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=561967#post561967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm..... I've been collecting comics for over 40 years. I have files cabinets full of them. I also have advanced degrees in anthropology with an emphasis in comparative mythology. I would argue very emphatically that there has been LESS change in the past 10-15 years than there was between the two decades before that..<br /> <br /> I stand by what I said EXACTLY. The example given was: Superman gets charged up by Apollo's &quot;sun blast&quot; and uses the energy to punch him through a mountain. In what way does that represent Superman as anything other than what I said he was while simultaneously not representing Apollo as anything other than another type of similar super-being?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Superman could have punched him through a mountain <i>before</i> getting blasted? The fact that this version of Apollo seems to be a representation of ALL Earth's Sun-Gods? (Writer Brian Azarello has more or else stated as much in interviews, that all deities in this story are essentially the sentient manifestations of the concepts they represent.) And to clarify, I was not implying ignorance on your part, merely seeking to gauge your knowledge of currant events.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.dccomics.com/comics/superman-wonder-woman-2013/supermanwonder-woman-1\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dccomics.com/comics/super...wonder-woman-1</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:27:19-07:00","id":562443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562005#post562005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its worth mentioning that the introduction of deities to comic books in Marvels Thor was originally intended by Stan Lee (First of his name) to explicitly be better than Superman could ever be and frankly to kick his ass all over the place. The entire inspiration was &quot;What could be more powerful than Superman? Someone who isn't a Man at all, but a living God&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, this runs into reality when large segments of the populace are uncomfortable with letting their children read about and Idealize other Deities and the general fact that Superman is the most popular hero in the world, at the end of the day narrative reality bows to that other super powerful green item.<br /> <br /> I'll also bring up the fact that Superman and many other comic book characters are religious in some vague manner (I think Superman might be a Methodist, the Thing is Jewish, etc). that means they acknowledge the presence of Deities, that they are more powerful than them and even deserving of worship from them. That kinda solidifies the issue in my mind as the Deities in Scion are not literary figures who happen to have taken an ancient name, but the honest to goodness Gods of the worlds religions. (Including the ones superheros might worship)</div> </div> </div> </div>A few years back, someone asked Thor about this kind of thing. He said that there was a realm even more glorious than Asgard, and that the God who dwelt there was greater than him...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T19:12:05-07:00","id":562503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562439#post562439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that Superman could have punched him through a mountain <i>before</i> getting blasted? The fact that this version of Apollo seems to be a representation of ALL Earth's Sun-Gods? (Writer Brian Azarello has more or else stated as much in interviews, that all deities in this story are essentially the sentient manifestations of the concepts they represent.) And to clarify, I was not implying ignorance on your part, merely seeking to gauge your knowledge of currant events.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.dccomics.com/comics/superman-wonder-woman-2013/supermanwonder-woman-1\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dccomics.com/comics/super...wonder-woman-1</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You're just proving the point more and more. There is no way that comic representation of Apollo or All-Sun-Gods-in-One-Greek-Package is something that flies when discussing mythology. It's &quot;dumbing&quot; the idea of mythology down to make it fit into a more narrow context, that of comodified serialized narratives. <br /> <br /> That's aside from the fact that Superman at least respects the Kryptonian deity Rao and Rao is a sun god, so technically, he just punched Rao through the mountain. So he respects, even worships, someone who is essentially and utterly his bitch? Nah... <br /> <br /> When Superman was REALLY powerful, meaning god levels of power (knows all, sees all, remembers all, can kick planets out of orbit, etc.) , they had to retcon away most of his power. They have done so again and again.... With him and with other heroes when they &quot;go all godlike&quot; Kyle Rayner becomes omnipotent/omniscient, depower him. Etc.<br /> <br /> There are some comics that depict gods acting like gods doing godlike things with godlike levels of powers, but, in general, they are not really integrated into the same genre that the Novas (Novae?) are depicting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:49:08-07:00","id":562564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562503#post562503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're just proving the point more and more. There is no way that comic representation of Apollo or All-Sun-Gods-in-One-Greek-Package is something that flies when discussing mythology. It's &quot;dumbing&quot; the idea of mythology down to make it fit into a more narrow context, that of comodified serialized narratives.<br /> <br /> That's aside from the fact that Superman at least respects the Kryptonian deity Rao and Rao is a sun god, so technically, he just punched Rao through the mountain. So he respects, even worships, someone who is essentially and utterly his bitch? Nah...<br /> <br /> When Superman was REALLY powerful, meaning god levels of power (knows all, sees all, remembers all, can kick planets out of orbit, etc.) , they had to retcon away most of his power. They have done so again and again.... With him and with other heroes when they &quot;go all godlike&quot; Kyle Rayner becomes omnipotent/omniscient, depower him. Etc.<br /> <br /> There are some comics that depict gods acting like gods doing godlike things with godlike levels of powers, but, in general, they are not really integrated into the same genre that the Novas (Novae?) are depicting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. My point was that Trinity and Scion characters SHOULD seem about the same power-wise, if the are at the same level. (I don't know what the Legend analog for Novas[Novi?] is.)<br /> <br /> But about Rao? I did say EARTH'S gods, not Krypton's. I'll shut up now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-21-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T00:33:01-07:00","id":562728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562443#post562443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few years back, someone asked Thor about this kind of thing. He said that there was a realm even more glorious than Asgard, and that the God who dwelt there was greater than him...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is Christianity pandering, where people have to include a greater god so that Christians don't get annoyed at all the gods running around without representation from 'their one true god' as the biggest and goddiest of them all. Although it is funny to think of it as referring to Superman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T02:50:43-07:00","id":562775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562728#post562728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is Christianity pandering, where people have to include a greater god so that Christians don't get annoyed at all the gods running around without representation from 'their one true god' as the biggest and goddiest of them all. Although it is funny to think of it as referring to Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually specifically addressed that in my second paragraph. The original vision of Thor was to make him be THE god of Thunder, that was his concept. The latter rewrites just muck with this because people are uncomfortable with a Deity being presented so you get various things like him being an alien or some kind of lesser hierarchy God, despite him routinely referring to himself as an Immortal Deity.<br /> <br /> My point was that its a matter of narrative cohesion. In the world of comic books which Novas are based on, deities and religions exist and are even commonly worshiped by even the greatest of heros despite their sometimes godlike abilities. This is because as Ajax mentioned earlier, the Feats and powers of a God cannot truely be simulated with mechanics as its trancendent and is incomparable to Novas. We use rules to simulate them because this is a game, but that means that the two worlds are pretty incompatible, one of the realities needs to break to accomodate the other and its going to be the Nova reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T09:32:10-07:00","id":563076,"title":"","content":"The idea of a greatest, omnipotent deity (usually a creator) is actually part of many many mythologies around the world (something that was/is used to great effect by missionaries). Typically, this deity is so &quot;above-it-all&quot; that it's nigh impossible to appeal to him or her through worship. You can and in many cases should and do, but you don't expect much in the way of attention coming the other direction. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, there can be a one-god-above-all-others, but that one deity is definitely one with a reciprocal relationship with his or her worshipers. It often comes in various flavors of which monotheism (this deity is the only deity) is the strongest (and the one the most difficult to handle in Scion). There's monolatry (there are other deities, but WE only worship this one) and henotheism (there are many gods but this one is the greatest among them but is still very much a god who is interested in mortal-ish things). <br /> <br /> So, saying such things doesn't HAVE to be pandering to the religious beliefs of the typical consumer. It doesn't really apply with respect to Thor. None of the above is a &quot;thing&quot; (in our sense, not the Norse one) with the Norse gods.<br /> <br /> When gods appear in most comics, having them fit into the constraints of comic reality only makes sense. So, in terms of Superman fighting Apollo (Uber-Sun-God form or not), it makes perfect comic book sense that can be parity between them. In science fiction and comics, gods fit within the conceits of the setting. In comics, most gods are pretty much superhero level entities. They may be &quot;magical&quot; beings. They may be aliens. They may be both. But they work at the level of the narrative to which they belong. There may be gods that transcend those levels. Odin does so from time to time in Marvel. Zeus sometimes does in DC. Both are effectively &quot;weakly godlike entities&quot;. But the conceit also applies to others and there are characters with levels of power that can be considered Titan-like from Scion (Galactus leaps to mind). Characters with godlike levels of power that aren't gods: anyone with the Power Cosmic at high levels who is not being a wuss (looks at Silver Surfer), Lanterns operating at the highest levels of power &amp; the Guardiants of the Universe, anyone holding on to the Cosimic Cube, the Ultimate Nullifier or able to wield one of the Infinity Gems, etc.<br /> <br /> However, those conceits and power levels were not really in play in Aberrant except for a few exceptions that toed that line (Divis Mal). Which is why my original concern. If new Aberrant is like old Aberrant setting-wise, then the gods of new Scion are going to be substantially powered down from those of old Scion based on the comment I mentioned in the OP. It seems like both settings are going to be cramped and crimped if Novas are god-level or higher. Either Novas are getting A LOT more powerful or gods are being wussified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:02:40-07:00","id":563086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=563076#post563076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either Novas are getting A LOT more powerful or gods are being wussified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=559676#post559676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't read too much into comparisons between the two universes right now. The benchmarks we're using only take into account internal playtesting, and we haven't brought actual powers into play yet, which are going to make a big difference in what characters can accomplish and what areas they can compete in.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not an arms race between Trinity and Scion. They're based on the same engine, but aren't being designed for PvP versus each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's way too early in the dev process, and we (the non-devs) have seen far too little to be overly concerned about the relative power levels of the top power levels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:38:14-07:00","id":563581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=562564#post562564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point. My point was that Trinity and Scion characters SHOULD seem about the same power-wise, if the are at the same level. (I don't know what the Legend analog for Novas[Novi?] is.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see most of Trinity being about Legend 1-4, with high powered Novas going up into Legend 5-7. But unless they changed the power level of the game dramatically and added a bunch of Living Tribunal level people into Trinity, even Divis Mal should cap out around Legend 8-9 at most (putting aside the universe creation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:13:19-07:00","id":564177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=563086#post563086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's way too early in the dev process, and we (the non-devs) have seen far too little to be overly concerned about the relative power levels of the top power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is based on a comment from the lead developer. Which is explicitly line v. line and definitely describes a power balance between the top end of the two lines. That is absolutely, most certainly something on which the non-developers can, and should, have an opinion, particularly early in the development process. Not that a non-developer can't and shouldn't have an opinion about any aspect of a game at any time, but, an Open Development situation is a specific invitation to have such and voice them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:19:17-07:00","id":564184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564177#post564177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thread is based on a comment from the lead developer. Which is explicitly line v. line and definitely describes a power balance between the top end of the two lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have missed part of the discussion because they have stated that the names are placeholders and nothing more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/537689-codename-sardonyx-teasers?p=559212#post559212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we keep saying, the names for tiers (and some mechanics) are placeholders, ready to be naturalized into Trinity or Scion. Getting hung up on the name for the top scale when neither game will present the scale table like that isn't really useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4074-sreden","name":"Sreden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:51:29-07:00","id":564204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564177#post564177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that a non-developer can't and shouldn't have an opinion about any aspect of a game at any time, but, an Open Development situation is a specific invitation to have such and voice them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we in an Open Dev situation? I've seen teasers, but the other OD processes have included an announcement of how / where / what to comment on. I assumed this was just sneak peeks at the underlying mechanics that will eventually become the Trinity Continuum and Scion -- projects that I assumed would have formal open dev periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T10:27:45-07:00","id":564257,"title":"","content":"This whole conversation is why I was skeptical about making these two games compatible. To quote the wisdom of the great Dr. Spengler, &quot;Don't cross the streams. It would be bad.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:23:48-07:00","id":564346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564177#post564177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thread is based on a comment from the lead developer. Which is explicitly line v. line and definitely describes a power balance between the top end of the two lines. That is absolutely, most certainly something on which the non-developers can, and should, have an opinion, particularly early in the development process. Not that a non-developer can't and shouldn't have an opinion about any aspect of a game at any time, but, an Open Development situation is a specific invitation to have such and voice them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aii-yaaaa.<br /> <br /> I was mostly making an example to describe the Scale system for individuals like the Colony (who nebulously create entire species from themselves, and may or may not be a Necromorph moon) and Divis Mal (who, yes, creates universes and takes his ball and goes home) compared to Hermes or even Bishamonten/Vi\u015brava\u1e47a. And that guy's a king.<br /> <br /> If you like, put Fenris, J\u00f6rmungandr, World Turtle, or Damballa around the same level. It's not meant to describe a ceiling, only an <i>extremely rough </i>benchmark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a comparison. The &quot;Aberrant&quot; designator, as I said, might describe those such as the Colony or Divis Mal; the &quot;God&quot; designator doesn't necessarily describe how Helios drives the chariot of the sun, or how Atlas holds up the World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole conversation is why I was skeptical about making these two games compatible. To quote the wisdom of the great Dr. Spengler, &quot;Don't cross the streams. It would be bad.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a driver for me to simply remove all designators from the document entirely, so yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:49:32-07:00","id":564455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564346#post564346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a driver for me to simply remove all designators from the document entirely, so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion. Description by feat, or setting neutral term, might be better idea in this case, for future reference.(Best might be description by popular non-universe character, which should fall into the tier, but I do not know, if that is allowed by law) On the other hand You will not get rid of this type of discussion, which will simply move to discuss/nitpick different aspect, so I do not think there is possible good outcome, just least annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:12:35-07:00","id":564800,"title":"","content":"This sounds more and more like the discussions that kids have in comic book stores about who can beat who in a fight when both characters are never going to meet. I, personally, prefer novas over gods but that is because I enjoy the Aeoniverse more than the Scion game. So, if you ask me? I would say that novas would win. If you ask a friend of mine who prefers Scion to the Aeoniverse? Then his answer would definitely be the gods. Which one of us is right? To those who say &quot;Neither of you&quot; then you are the winner of this debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:00:43-07:00","id":564974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564800#post564800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds more and more like the discussions that kids have in comic book stores about who can beat who in a fight when both characters are never going to meet. I, personally, prefer novas over gods but that is because I enjoy the Aeoniverse more than the Scion game. So, if you ask me? I would say that novas would win. If you ask a friend of mine who prefers Scion to the Aeoniverse? Then his answer would definitely be the gods. Which one of us is right? To those who say &quot;Neither of you&quot; then you are the winner of this debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with preferring Novas over Scions, or Scions over Novas. But who would win in a fight? That depends on who is fighting who.<br /> Superman is on a completely different power level than Wolverine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T01:18:15-07:00","id":565087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564974#post564974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with preferring Novas over Scions, or Scions over Novas. But who would win in a fight? That depends on who is fighting who.<br /> Superman is on a completely different power level than Wolverine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, Superman can only be on ONE superhero team at a time.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, what we are doing is trying to compare two things that have vaguely defined limits. If Superman went against the god of being Thor (also known as Thor) then it depends on where you cap Superman's strength (if I remember, Superman is officially 'as strong as he needs to be', and it's mainly his versatility that's limited) and how transcendent you make Thor's power.<br /> <br /> With Superman vs. Wolverine, do we have a definition of when Wolverine's healing factor stops working? If so, how often do he and Superman need to eat? Because though I agree that they are vastly different levels, we might end up with 'Superman attacks Wolverine until Logan stops healing or Supes runs out of energy' situation, where the winner is decided by who can last longer (my money is on the living solar cell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T01:32:13-07:00","id":565091,"title":"","content":"Well Wolverine got himself ripped in half and that didn't stop him turning up in more issues.<br /> <br /> Also, superman <i>could</i> be on multiple teams at once if he wanted<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://oyster.ignimgs.com/wordpress/stg.ign.com/2015/02/Tiny-Superman-2-thumb-550x523.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:07:19-07:00","id":565505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564204#post564204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are we in an Open Dev situation? I've seen teasers, but the other OD processes have included an announcement of how / where / what to comment on. I assumed this was just sneak peeks at the underlying mechanics that will eventually become the Trinity Continuum and Scion -- projects that I assumed would have formal open dev periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says that it is in the weekly bulletin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T10:11:14-07:00","id":565509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sreden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=564184#post564184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you have missed part of the discussion because they have stated that the names are placeholders and nothing more.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what your point with that statement is, particularly the &quot;nothing more&quot; part. Placeholders are useless without value. The names and terms used have value. Therefore having a discussion about what those placeholders represent is a valid exercise. They indicate the intent of the developers. The original question is phrased to seek an assessment from the community at large about the intent indicated in the statement and how they feel about it's implications in the development of both product lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/mem