t; in regards to Marvel / DC with a straight face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:21:44-07:00","id":567884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=567863#post567863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it amazing that anyone can discuss &quot;canon&quot; in regards to Marvel / DC with a straight face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we should discuss cannon instead, ideally, how big of one is needed to take down Novas and Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:35:36-07:00","id":568008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=567884#post567884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe we should discuss cannon instead, ideally, how big of one is needed to take down Novas and Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that Hephaestus already built a better one centuries ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:13:54-07:00","id":568516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=568008#post568008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember that Hephaestus already built a better one centuries ago</div> </div> </div> </div>E.E. &quot;Doc&quot; Smith Solar System cannon? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:23:58-07:00","id":579364,"title":"","content":"How do you really define a &quot;god&quot; anyway? Is it origin? Some cultures have gods who were born mortal. to mortal parents, yet ascended to godhood nonetheless. Is it stories? Some Pantheons have deities who have few if any feats of legend. Is it fame? Many modern celebrities are known to more people today than some cultures had members during their entire history. Is it age? Then your Scion really can't be a &quot;god&quot; until he or she has at least outlived a Mortal span of years. Is it worship? Depending on how you define the term &quot;worship&quot;, all <i>kinds</i> of things could be considered &quot;gods&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's power. Can they move mountains, command the elements, heal the sick, know the future, turn night into day,(or vice versa) make the deserts bloom, raise the dead? Then maybe it doesn't matter <b>HOW</b> they are able do these things, it only matters that they <b>CAN</b> do them.<br /> <br /> Again I don't pretend to be an expert on Trinity. I've barely glanced at one book. But based on what's been said in this thread, and my knowledge of what's possible in Scion at Legend 12, I think maybe the differences become <u>academic</u>. The Colony can spawn new races? Health Purview + Animal, Fertility, or Chaos. Divas Mal can make universes? So can a Chaos god, with a handful of Dark Matter and enough successes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T23:56:58-07:00","id":581997,"title":"","content":"By raw Scions (Atleast in 1E, which might be irrelevant here) become gods by becoming more metaphysically potent and important in the grand scheme of the universe. Worship and fame have nothing to do with it. It also requires descent from a God at some point as the heritage is literally a part of your blood. A mortal cannot become super famous or skilled and ascend to godhood (Though individual pantheons might make them lesser supernatural creatures or bless them with powers).<br /> <br /> Actually, if we take scion rules into consideration, A god who is roughly equal with a Nova should still triumph when they use an epic attribute, (which is effectively an I win button and the mechanical interaction of this) because they are simply more metaphysically important than some mortal with nifty superpowers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Colony can spawn new races? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Divas Mal can make universes? </div> </div> </div>Its worth noting that many if not most of the Deities in Scion did stuff like that on accident, on a flippant bet, or in the course of natural body processes (Shout out to Ptah).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T16:18:27-07:00","id":582836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=581997#post581997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By raw Scions (Atleast in 1E, which might be irrelevant here) become gods by becoming more metaphysically potent and important in the grand scheme of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;metaphysically potent&quot;. The term &quot;metaphysical&quot; is, at best, hard to quantify, almost by definition.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=581997#post581997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Worship and fame have nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The persistent use of the word &quot;Legend&quot; undermines that premise a bit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=581997#post581997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It also requires descent from a God at some point as the heritage is literally a part of your blood. A mortal cannot become super famous or skilled and ascend to godhood (Though individual pantheons might make them lesser supernatural creatures or bless them with powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>From the &quot;Fluff&quot; as written, Izanami and Izanagi were just normal humans at first, as were some member of the Celestial Bureaucracy, as I recall. (I don't have the books with me) Just because there's no game mechanic for something, doesn't mean it never happens.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=581997#post581997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if we take scion rules into consideration, A god who is roughly equal with a Nova should still triumph when they use an epic attribute, (which is effectively an I win button and the mechanical interaction of this) because they are simply more metaphysically important than some mortal with nifty superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't know Trinity very well, but don't they have similar attribute boosts?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T05:48:26-07:00","id":583411,"title":"","content":"We really need to have a better definition of Legend, I see it as being a mixture about importance to the story Fate is weaving, and how influential you are among mortals. Somebody who is barely known won't achieve Demigod status unless his deeds start impacting the world and mortals start knowing him (whether by name or description, you can rise to Godhood as both Joe Blogs and 'the guy with the lightning gun' [okay, I actually kind of like Eric conceptually, I just wish he had some Epic Dex and Epic Perception]), no matter how much of the main character he is to the universe (it'll likely end up dropping him in favour of someone with more Fatebindings).<br /> <br /> And Novas have Mega-Attributes, which are conceptually similar to Epics, but I think worth 5 autosuccesses (or maybe 5 dice, been a while since I read the book, it isn't clear), giving the ruling of 'the higher Mega-Attribute always wins'. I actually prefer Epics, I just don't like how they scale (it makes difficulties hard to adjudicate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:00:47-07:00","id":583472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=582836#post582836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;metaphysically potent&quot;. The term &quot;metaphysical&quot; is, at best, hard to quantify, almost by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Of or relating to the transcendent or to a reality beyond what is perceptible to the senses&quot;. By definition, the gods are not famous people, they are beings of strength, importance and power with metaphysical ties to the very nature of reality and beyond. These are not superheros, they are actually Fire and Brimstone Deities in the &quot;I am the lord thy God&quot; variety. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The persistent use of the word &quot;Legend&quot; undermines that premise a bit. </div> </div> </div>While a bit confusing terminology, the strength of a god has nothing to do with how well he is known or whether he is worshiped. Deities from long dead cultures and religions are still present. People did not create the gods through belief or worship, it was the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the &quot;Fluff&quot; as written, Izanami and Izanagi were just normal humans at first, as were some member of the Celestial Bureaucracy, as I recall. (I don't have the books with me) Just because there's no game mechanic for something, doesn't mean it never happens. </div> </div> </div>All Scions are normal people until their parent visits them and activates the latent power in their blood. Alternatively, if the scions parent formally disinherits them in &quot;The Heavens&quot; then another Deity may &quot;Adopt&quot; them. It still requires actual descent from a deity unless your using houserules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I don't know Trinity very well, but don't they have similar attribute boosts? </div> </div> </div>Up to the Ultimate attribute gods receive, yes. Once they max their Epics the next boost comes in the form of a narrative example of their ultimate ability. Someone with ultimate stamina survives any attack, someone with ultimate strength lifts anything or kills anything, etc. Its less mechanical and more narrative at that point. (Same with Avatars)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:03:03-07:00","id":583474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=583411#post583411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We really need to have a better definition of Legend, I see it as being a mixture about importance to the story Fate is weaving, and how influential you are among mortals. Somebody who is barely known won't achieve Demigod status unless his deeds start impacting the world and mortals start knowing him (whether by name or description, you can rise to Godhood as both Joe Blogs and 'the guy with the lightning gun'</div> </div> </div> </div>Being known is not a prerequisite for legend rise. Fate knows your actions and the &quot;Truth&quot; of the event and that's all that matters.<br /> <br /> Also, By Raw, Being famous and influential among mortals provides no metaphysical boost to a Hero, Demigod or God. Mortals actively worshiping you provides you with nothing but the satisfaction of a job well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:19:38-07:00","id":583482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559551-novas-v-gods?p=583474#post583474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being known is not a prerequisite for legend rise. Fate knows your actions and the &quot;Truth&quot; of the event and that's all that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and I'm not happy with this, partially because otherwise players have no incentive not to keep up a Masquerade, whereas I want a more World of Awesome than World of Shadow Lurking. I also really do not get why it's called Legend because it has nothing to do with the word (either 'a traditional story sometimes popularly regarded as historical but not authenticated' or 'very well known'), unless the designers just wanted it to represent 'Legendaryness'. Needing the players to get some people knowing of them to increase in power hit two birds with one stone, and I prefer it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, By Raw, Being famous and influential among mortals provides no metaphysical boost to a Hero, Demigod or God. Mortals actively worshiping you provides you with nothing but the satisfaction of a job well done. </div> </div> </div>Yep, this is bad, bad, bad. I think that the rules definitely need to support this, with a difference between being known (which I have pegged as raising Legend), and being worshipped (which I'd make a version of the followers background for who aren't available, but provide a steady stream of 1 Legend per worshipper per day). Then those who want mortal worship to do nothing can just ban the Cult background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:22:24-07:00","id":583531,"title":"","content":"I totally 100% disagree. With that thinking almost ALL of the pantheons in Scion should be starved scattered remnants of their former glory. Currently worshipped pantheons would dominate the game, most of which would be almost completely unknown to most Western audiences (meaning '&quot;the people who are buying the products&quot;), followed by a few pantheons that are embedded as cultural archetypes who, arguably have no actual worshippers (or, at least, their current worshippers have no continuity with the original cultures associated with the pantheons).<br /> <br /> So you have a world with powerful Chinese and Indian pantheons, a healthy Japanese and Voodoo pantheon, an anemic Aztec pantheon kept around by some minor and largely unacknowledged syncretism recognized soly by academics. Greek and Norse pantheons surviving on the equivalent of magical methadone. Egypt and Mesopotamian? Dead. They weren't worshiped or even really known about for 1000s of years. And the really really powerful &quot;pantheons&quot; would be Islam and Christianity. And so very many other interesting pantheons either around, but probably not all that powerful, like the Orisha (who have a chunk of people who still worship them, but nothing at all like what you see with the Hindu pantheon) or almost completely wiped out by missionaries in the past 5 centuries. (Bye bye Polynesian pantheons, etc.)<br /> <br /> The whole idea of gods deriving their powers from the amount of worship they receive has absolutely no value in the context of actual myths. Zeus doesn't care if you believe in him. He's REAL. He's THERE. And he's got LIGHTNING BOLTS to hurl at you if you piss him off. Heroes who do mighty deeds in mythology don't do them in front of audiences to bolster their powers. We humans tell storiedsabout them, but they don't NEED us to do so. We do it because they are awesome, powerful and dangerous. Are tigers more dangerous because everyone knows about them? Are cone snails less dangerous? Nope. In fact cone snails are MUCH more deadly than tigers, they just don't look sexy and get good press. <br /> <br /> The whole concept of worship gives the gods power is a very modern conceit that has definitely been perpetuated by RPGs and has something of a foothold in modern fantasy (all the way back to L. Sprague deCamp, so it's distinguished lineage), though there are many many games out there where it never even showed up. D&amp;D Immortals - power increase due to deeds, not worshipers, RuneQuest - gods are gods are gods (are trees are moons are continents), Etc. <br /> <br /> But Scion is supposed to be about taking the ancient myths and bringing them into modern times. Not about taking modern concepts and retconing ancient myths. (Well, okay, there is definitely that, but not in the context addressed herein.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:01:02-07:00","id":583556,"title":"","content":"I had a long post about my reasoning for the getting known thing, until I had a better idea. Instead of stories increasing Legend, Legend increases stories. This makes it so that if Ra ever came down to Earth and beat up a Legend 11 Titanspawn everybody will be talking about it (as it is, he's fighting in the overworld and being talked about by mythological creatures). This mainly works by fatebinding.<br /> <br /> Also, on the worshippers front, I really am going to use it, but possibly at 1 point per day per dot of cult per day, max 5. At this point it's useful for Heroes and Demigods, but due to the natural Legend Point regeneration mechanics I'm using (Legend per Scene plus a full refresh per day at either Dawn or Dusk) it's a blip in a God's pool. If Thor is waking up with 148 Legend points every morning, is getting 12 per scene and can regain more by stunting, do you think he cares that some Indian god has 5 Legend points once per day? The Aztecs get a lot more out of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:27:13-07:00","id":583573,"title":"","content":"Based on the rational in the last paragraph, why do I, as a Hero or Demigod care about those worshippers? They don't do jack for me. No matter how huge my cult is, I can top that amount of Legend points by 3 reasonably cool stunts. <br /> <br /> The real problem with this system It also adds in a lot of persnickity book-keeping. You will need to keep track of every day passing to see how many Legend points are regained. Which isn't the problem, really. That also matters for Willpower. The real problem is if there are temporally long periods of downtime during an adventure. In which case getting 5 points of Legend every day starts to matter a lot. If Thor is getting 0 or 1 Legend point/day and Indra is getting 5 , that begins to MATTER, very fast. Thor gets 0 or 30 Legend back in the same time period that Vishnu gets all 144 back with 6 to spare, even though they are both riding the same boring train from Amsterdam to Vladivostok (to get from the head of the &quot;amalgamated World Serpents&quot;. to the tip of its tail and NOT awaken it have it rip the world apart by doing Legendary things) . And stunting isn't really a thing that occurs in most downtime (or else it's probably not downtime). Now take those same numbers for Heroes with Max Legend point pools of 16. A couple of days is a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:37:08-07:00","id":583680,"title":"","content":"First off, the idea is that a Hero can easily find himself low in Legend just from using powers, so a handful of extra Legend can mean the difference between life and death and few some powers on their level. I will say that the rules aren't playtested, and won't be for a while.<br /> <br /> I'm confused at the 'by the time Thor has regained 0 or 30 Legend Points', by the time you get the points from Cult you gain a full refresh. This is so the points don't stack, if I have used 3 of my 5 points from it by the time I refresh my legend, I get access to 5 points which I can pull into my Legend Pool. If I use none of them, the next day I have 5 (and a full Legend Pool). I can see the potential for problems, which is why I intend to playtest the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:26:21-07:00","id":583833,"title":"","content":"Since we don't have the new rules or if there will even be Legend, that's effectively a moot discussion. <br /> <br /> If you can't see the problem with a Birthright that recharges characters that sit on their asses and do nothing godly except passively be worshiped, I don't think we're seeing this game the same way at all. Not just in the sense of how the game plays out, with the children of the gods doing epic mythical things, instead of cultivating their images like bureaucratic Kardashians. But you are missing a big glaring flaw in your design. There is a lot of discussion about Iztli being overpowered due to way it allows the Aztecs excessive access to Legend points. This is system is much much worse. <br /> <br /> Once again: If I have a Legend 4 Hero with a Cult of 5 who goes down to 1 Legend, I can run away and do absolutely nothing for 3 days and be at full power. Now, that may not make of a difference if the adventure in question is one where minutes count, but if it's one where days of downtime can pass between action scenes (which has happened frequently in games I have played in and in ones I have run), that is an enormous advantage. My Legend 4 Hero companions with Cult 0 get NO Legend back for sitting on their asses like I am. <br /> <br /> This system incentivizes inaction and de-incentivizes stunting to get Legend. Which is subset of de-incentivizing action. If inaction nets positive results, it's going to happen, because it will be a smart thing for a player to do to have his character at his/her most effective. At least the Aztecs (or users of Magic) have to DO SOMETHING to get all that Legend, and that something has consequences.<br /> <br /> And that's besides the fact that getting power from worship just isn't in Scion's wheelhouse. It was deliberately set up that way (with a few problematic bits that have been admitted to have gotten by the final edit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:17:20-07:00","id":583970,"title":"","content":"It's a houserule for a specific purpose beyond the scope of this thread (but basically, you don't get power from worship so much as it being a weird fatebind like thing, I haven't worked out all the details).<br /> <br /> Oh, and I'm using variant Legend regen rules to ease players into the idea of stunting. As I explained, sitting on your arse wastes the legend, but to explain clearly:<br /> -at dawn, dusk, noon, midnight or other appropriate time of the day (chosen at character generation or by me for the Chronicle), refresh all Legend Points. This is to ensure that characters have access to Legend even if they've been inactive while dry recently.<br /> -at the end of the scene, take a number of Legend Points equal to your Legend (this will be later removed in favour of encouraging Stunts).<br /> -once per day, you can add points to your current Legend Pool equal to your rating in cult. As a free action.<br /> <br /> Sitting on your arse gains you nothing extra from having a Cult. I decensitise sitting on your arse as much as I can anyway, and don't see how giving the enemy time to prepare in exchange for a full Legend Pool is not significant.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Cult power is to explain why you might willingly get minor fatebindings in exchange for power. As a side note, I've completely rewritten the low-level Itzli powers already because they really aren't useful except as a stepping stone. Cult cannot be bought at character creation or with experience and is meant to flucuate but is a Birthright because there are no backgrounds. I'm on the fence about actually properly writing the system (which would point out that building a Cult is not a very nice thing), partially because I don't have players who'll use it anyway. I'm tired of this, but the argument is my fault because I hate typing on my phone and so neglected to mention that I WANT A REASON FOR SCIONS TO WANT TO BECOME KNOWN. But as you obviously can't actually read what I write without jumping to 'it makes those with cults inclined to do nothing', whereas it just provids an 'oh crap' option that gives no significant boost to a god's power (intentionally, to explain why gods aren't concerned with setting up thousand strong cults).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}